  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x. \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0)) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
